      {
        "Id": "5d113508a4584ea1b51c0d634a78556b",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  open the floor plan with the stair drawn in Revit lines (model / detail) or in a CAD linked / imported in the plan (select lines first = only those) - or set 0 = AREA to use the Area / Room named STAIR (lines inside it, else an automatic layout).  A flight = 3+ parallel tread lines; flights close together = one stair with landings; the walk-line arrow = UP (or Flip).  Floor to floor from the plan level to the next level (3) or a height (4).  FIT (6) = riser (7) / tread (8) inside the drawn outline; LINES = one riser per line, NOT built when the riser is over 5.  Repeat (11) = the same stair on the floors above.  RUN False = preview.  Run again = replaced (no doubles).",
        "DescriptionText": "",
        "IsExpanded": true,
